# msil-env.ps1 trusts the x64 developer environment that lit passes on (plan
# section 12, M26; CI run 41257850076's failure of gtest.test): lit drops
# VSCMD_ARG_TGT_ARCH and gives each run a fresh TEMP, but passes PATH,
# INCLUDE, LIB and VSINSTALLDIR on, so a script that dot-sources
# msil-env.ps1 under lit must see the x64 cl.exe on PATH and use the loaded
# environment, not enter Visual Studio again (which on CI imported the
# DevShell module of a Visual Studio that the runner does not have). The
# evidence is TEMP: entering the developer shell caches what it changed in
# %TEMP%\msil-vsenv-x64.json, and trusting the loaded one writes nothing.
# (1) A passing msil-gtest.ps1 case (the fake program of gtest.test) with
# TEMP and TMP set to an empty directory passes, and that directory holds no
# msil-vsenv-x64.json afterwards.
# (2) The failure path: the same case with every directory that holds a
# cl.exe removed from PATH is not a loaded environment, so msil-env.ps1
# enters the developer shell of the Visual Studio root (VSINSTALLDIR, else
# vswhere's) and writes msil-vsenv-x64.json into that TEMP; the case still
# passes. msil-ucrt-headers (INCLUDE names the UCRT headers) means lit runs
# in a developer environment, which (1) needs and (2) re-enters.
# REQUIRES: system-windows, msil-netfx, pwsh, msil-ucrt-headers

# RUN: rm -rf %t.vsenv %t.novsenv %t.build && mkdir -p %t.vsenv %t.novsenv
# RUN: %ilasm -exe -output=%t.fake.exe %S/Inputs/fake-program.il

# (1)
# RUN: env TEMP=%t.vsenv TMP=%t.vsenv FAKE_PROGRAM_OUTPUT=%S/Inputs/fake-output/gtest-passed-3.txt FAKE_PROGRAM_STATUS=0 %{harness_check} exits 0 %{harness_gtest} -BuildDir %t.build -Exe %t.fake.exe -Filter "MSILFake.*" -NoSkip -MinTests 3
# RUN: %{harness_check} missing %t.vsenv/msil-vsenv-x64.json

# (2)
# RUN: env TEMP=%t.novsenv TMP=%t.novsenv FAKE_PROGRAM_OUTPUT=%S/Inputs/fake-output/gtest-passed-3.txt FAKE_PROGRAM_STATUS=0 %{harness_check} exits 0 pwsh -NoProfile -NonInteractive -Command "$env:PATH = @($env:PATH -split ';' | Where-Object { $_ -and -not (Test-Path -LiteralPath (Join-Path $_ 'cl.exe')) }) -join ';'; if (Get-Command cl.exe -ErrorAction SilentlyContinue) { exit 9 }; & '%S/../../utils/build/msil-gtest.ps1' -BuildDir '%t.build' -Exe '%t.fake.exe' -Filter 'MSILFake.*' -NoSkip -MinTests 3; exit $LASTEXITCODE"
# RUN: %{harness_check} contains %t.novsenv/msil-vsenv-x64.json "\"vars\""
